components.description:
Grid 26px | 1fr | auto.
- 16×16 checkbox button (aria-label 'Toggle'): border 1.5px, radius 3px, check glyph 13px with the same transitions as the 18px variant.
- Text: 13px; the item text with done styling + ' · <sub>' in muted. The sub is 'BD3' for BAU rows or the project short name for project rows.
- Due label in mono 11px:
  - done: 'done 5 Oct' (--ink-faint, 400);
  - overdue: 'overdue N BD' (color-mix(risk 45%, ink), 600);
  - due today: 'today' (--ink, 600);
  - otherwise 'Thu 15 Oct' (--ink-muted, 400).

Milestone rows prefix the text with '◆ '. Hover sets the global hover to the routine id or project id. Dims to 0.3.

Odometer-style rolling text; the prop is value (string). Used for fundsDone and mo.doneN.

Numeric values matching /^([+−-]?)(\d{1,3})(?:\.(\d))?(\D*)$/ are split into columns:
- a sign column (['', '+', '−']);
- 3 digit columns, left-padded with '' (empty cells collapse to zero width);
- a '.' column;
- a one-decimal digit column;
- a static suffix.

Date values like 'Wed 2 Dec' roll the weekday, digits and month.

Each column is a 1.25em-tall overflow:hidden window. Inside it is a vertical stack of all possible cells, translated by translateY(-index×1.25em) with transition: transform var(--dur-slow) var(--spring-soft), which is 440ms. A hidden copy of the full text sizes the element; the rolling layer is aria-hidden. Line-height 1.25, inline-block, baseline aligned.

dataConsumed:
model.F: formatter helpers keyed by day number. The ones Today uses:
- s(n) → 'Mon 5 Oct';
- dm(n) → '5 Oct';
- l(n) → 'Monday 5 October';
- mon(n) → 'Oct';
- monL(n) → 'October';
- d(n) → 5;
- iso(n) → '2026-10-05';
- dn(iso) → day number.

model.CAL: business-day calendar.
- days[n] = {n, iso, w (0=Sun), m (0-based month), d, y, bd (bool), bdm (BD index within the month, starting at 1, or null), hol (name or null)};
- bds: sorted array of business-day numbers;
- idx: map from day number to its index in bds;
- nextBD(n), addBD(n, k), bdDiff(a, b) = idx[nextBD(b)] − idx[nextBD(a)].

model.P: derived projects[]. Fields Today reads:
- id, name, short, goal;
- accent ('var(--pc-accent)' or 'var(--fi-accent)');
- domainName ('Private Credit' / 'Fixed Income');
- forecastN (number|null);
- now: [{m: milestoneName, due: iso, tasks: [{id, t: text, h: hours, due?: iso}]}];
- next: [{m, due}];
- milestones: derived and sorted [{name, date: iso}];
- forecastS, sinceLabel, checkin (these three feed only the unused prompt).

model.routines: derived routines[]. Fields:
- id, name, short, domain, kind ('monthly'|'weekly'|'daily'), bd, wd, h;
- stage (0 Manual, 1 Automating, 2 Shadowed, 3 Handed over), stageName;
- ruleShort ('BD8' | 'Weekly · Tue' | 'Daily');
- next: first 3 occurrences on or after TODAY, [{n, s, after, today}].

interactions:
Click a month-snapshot checkbox (only the 16px square is the button, not the whole row):
- the returns row for TODAY: m.setAllFunds(!allFundsDone), which ticks or unticks all 12 funds;
- any other BAU row: m.toggleBau('<routineId>:<iso>'), which stores the ISO of TODAY as the done date;
- a project task: m.toggleTask(id);
- a milestone row: m.toggleTask('ms:<pid>:<name>').

Hover (mouseenter) sets the global hover id, and mouseleave clears it with setHover(null). Hover sources:
- plan rows: the Returns card ('r-ret'), other BAU rows, focus blocks;
- capacity bar segments (except free);
- week mini-bar segments;
- week chips (a milestone chip uses its project id);
- week project items;
- month rows (routine id or project id).
Every element tied to a different id dims to opacity 0.3 (0.25 for bar segments), with a 140ms ease-out transition. Hover state lives in the shell, so it cross-highlights between the capacity bar, plan, week strip and month list.

Hover styles:
- week card background becomes ink 3.5% (via !important, so it also overrides the selected background);
- 'Routine' / 'Workspace' / 'Show more' buttons turn --ink (no transition);
- the 'Back to today' border turns --ink-faint.

motion:
Checkbox tick:
- background and border-color: 140ms ease-out;
- glyph opacity 0→1: 140ms ease-out;
- glyph scale 0.4→1: 180ms cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.5, 0.64, 1), an overshoot 'pop'. Under reduced motion the scale is always 1.
- Label colour: 240ms ease-out.
- Strike-through appears instantly.

algorithms:
dayLoad(n) (shell), computed for every BD.

BAU items:
- If n < MOVE: every routine with stage < 3 that occurs on n is added as {kind: 'bau', domain: 'pc' (hard-coded), h: r.h, name: r.short || r.name}.
- Otherwise: the rotation segment containing n gives {id: 'rot', kind: 'bau', domain: 'fi', h: 4, name: '<country> · <Build|Refresh>'}.

Project items: for each project with startN ≤ n ≤ (forecastN ?? targetN), take the first rule that applies:
1. h = p.ov[iso] if an override exists;
2. else if n ≥ MOVE, h = rateAfter;
3. else if bdm = 3, h = bd3;
4. else if bdm = 8, h = bd8;
5. else h = rate.
The item is added if h > 0.

Totals: bau = Σ BAU h, proj = Σ project h, total = bau + proj, free = max(0, 8 − total), over = total > 8.

backendImplications:
A Today/day-plan endpoint, e.g. GET /api/today?date=YYYY-MM-DD, returning:
- the header: date, bdm, monthBDs, kicker metadata, verdict;
- the load;
- the focus blocks: project, hours, the sliced tasks, the next milestone, and empty-state reason;
- other BAU rows;
- the next BAU run when the day has none.
The task-slicing algorithm (cumulative hours offset by earlier days' allocation from today) should run server-side or in a shared util, so Timeline/Calendar get the same answer.

risksAndQuirks:
Hard-coded copy and values in Today:
- '8h working day', 'of 8h planned', '…h of 8h' (it should use CAPACITY);
- the Returns card gutter '6h' (it should be the routine's h);
- 'BD3, monthly' (it should be the routine's ruleShort);
- 'of 12 funds' and fundsPct = done/12 (it should use FUNDS.length);
- 'BAU · Private Credit' on the Returns card;
- the '4h a day' fallback for the rotation.

localState:
Instance fields (not state):
- this.ft: day-switch timeout handle, cleared on unmount;
- this._req: the last dayReq.t handled.
